### What is the anyOf pitfall?

```java
CF<Object> first = CompletableFuture.anyOf(
    supplyAsync(() -> { throw new RuntimeException("Bureau-1 down!"); }),
    supplyAsync(() -> { sleep(200); return 750; }),
    supplyAsync(() -> { sleep(400); return 720; })
);
// anyOf returns Bureau-1's FAILURE (first to complete!)
// Bureau-2 would have succeeded, but anyOf already completed with error.
```

### How do you implement race-on-success?

```java
package com.bank.service;

import java.util.concurrent.*;
import java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicInteger;
import java.util.List;

public class RaceOnSuccess {
    public static <T> CompletableFuture<T> race(
            List<CompletableFuture<T>> futures, long timeoutMs) {

        CompletableFuture<T> result = new CompletableFuture<>();
        AtomicInteger remaining = new AtomicInteger(futures.size());

        for (CompletableFuture<T> cf : futures) {
            cf.whenComplete((value, ex) -> {
                if (ex == null) {
                    if (result.complete(value)) {
                        futures.forEach(f -> f.cancel(true));
                    }
                } else {
                    if (remaining.decrementAndGet() == 0 && !result.isDone()) {
                        result.completeExceptionally(ex);
                    }
                }
            });
        }

        result.orTimeout(timeoutMs, TimeUnit.MILLISECONDS);
        return result;
    }
}
```

### What is the trade-off?

N parallel calls = N times backend load. This is justified for latency-critical, revenue-impacting paths (checkout page, loan approval). Not justified for bulk background processing.

### What are the three outcomes?

| Outcome | What happens |
|---|---|
| First success | Result CF completed, others cancelled |
| All failed | Result CF completed exceptionally with last error |
| Timeout | Result CF completed with TimeoutException |

### What are common interview follow-up questions?

- Does cancel(true) actually stop the running task? It sets the interrupt flag, but the task must cooperate by checking isInterrupted() or being in a blocking call.
- When is hedged requesting worth the cost? When P99 latency directly impacts revenue (checkout, search, ads).
- How does this compare to Resilience4j Retry? Retry is sequential (try, wait, try again). Hedging is parallel (try all simultaneously).
